    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0653" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10754: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-27T18:00:00-05:00">October 27, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>270. Your 481, October 20, 4 p.m. According to an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> of October 26 from the British Embassy the British
                    Government has instructed the British Ambassador to make further representations
                    in regard to the use of the International Settlement as a base for Japanese
                    military operations.</p>
                <p>You are authorized after consultation with your British colleague to inform the
                    Japanese Government<anchor n="72" xml:id="d702-f1"/> that this Government
                    continues to hold the views as set forth in our 245, October 2, 3 p.m. (your <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of October 4).<anchor n="73"
                        xml:id="d702-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d702-f1" n="72" xml:id="d702-f1-content">
                <p>The British and American Embassies carried out similar instructions on October 27
                    and 28 respectively. For the American <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>,
                    see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_404"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 404</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d702-f2" n="73" xml:id="d702-f2-content">
                <p>For American <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of October 4, see <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_378"><hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., p.
                        378</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
